# OCR Mini App — durable worklog

## Goal

Add a safe OCR launcher to the existing Telegram Mini App at
`apps.bigalexn8n.ru` without duplicating OCR business logic.

## Agreed MVP

- The OCR card is visible to all Mini App users.
- Any user who opened the app through Telegram may start OCR.
- The server verifies signed Telegram `initData`; a public web request is denied.
- The source folder is fixed to the existing `протокол` folder.
- A dedicated screen shows readiness, active/last batch status, and a confirmed
  start action.
- The existing n8n/Postgres single-active-batch lock remains authoritative.
- OCR results and completion reports continue through the existing workflow.

## Architecture

`Mini App -> Apps Hub authenticated API -> protected n8n OCR batch webhook ->
Postgres queue -> local PaddleOCR -> Yandex Disk -> Telegram completion report`

Apps Hub receives only two runtime secrets through environment variables:
`TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN` for Telegram signature verification and
`OCR_BATCH_TRIGGER_TOKEN` for the existing protected n8n webhook. Secret values
must never be written to this worklog, source files, logs, or documentation.

## Verification checklist

- Valid signed Telegram init data is accepted; tampered, expired, and missing
  data are rejected.
- Anonymous HTTP callers cannot start OCR or inspect its operational status.
- Start calls the existing protected n8n webhook and preserves the requesting
  Telegram user as both `chat_id` and `requested_by`.
- Status reports OCR service health and the latest/active batch from Postgres.
- Existing `/ocr` tests still pass.
- Mini App works at mobile viewport, shows confirmation/loading/error states,
  and polls while a batch is active.
- Production smoke test does not start a new OCR batch; it checks auth rejection,
  app/API health, current queue status, and the existing 20/20 clean baseline.

## Resume protocol

At the start of a later session, read this file, inspect the files listed under
`Changed files`, then continue from `Next step`. Never assume deployment happened
unless the production checks are recorded below.

