  `@bibi_translation_review_bot`. The shared secret was aligned with the
  polling service and only `apps-hub` was recreated. Production verification:
  real-bot signed status returns 200, tampered and unsigned requests return 401,
  all 11 focused container tests pass, the OCR service is ready, and
  `ocr_status.sh` reports 20 `done` rows with an empty error table. No OCR batch
  was started.
- 2026-07-16: during the first real 101-221 batch, user acceptance found false
  ASCII `f1 1I` on page 106 and ellipses shifted outside their source position.
  Root cause: Paddle misread quotation marks around punctuation-only dialogue,
  while dot restoration mapped pixels to a uniform character count. The layout
  renderer now removes adjacent/inline quote artifacts (`f1`, `I`, `··`), wraps
  standalone ellipses, uses width-aware Hangul mapping, and keeps restored dots
  before the closing quote. Sixteen unit tests pass. Candidate OCR of pages 106
  and 145 matches the source
  layout: no `f1 1I`, standalone dots are quoted, and inline dots follow the
  correct syllable. The fixed image is deployed; the active batch continues.
  A quiet one-shot continuation was prepared for 02:10 MSK to verify completion,
  reprocess only pages 101-160, and validate the corrected TXT files. It was
  subsequently disabled when Алексей paused work until morning; unrelated legacy
  jobs account for the cron preflight warnings.
